================================================
PART 11 — MERGE CONFLICT
================================================

Example:
    git switch main
    git merge feature/signup

If Git reports a conflict:

1. Check conflicted files:
    git status

2. Open the conflicted file.

You may see markers like:
    <<<<<<< HEAD
    main version
    =======
    feature version
    >>>>>>> feature/signup

3. Edit the file and keep the correct code.
4. Remove all conflict markers.
5. Stage the resolved file:
    git add app.js

6. Complete the merge:
    git commit -m "Resolve merge conflict"

7. Push:
    git push

================================================
PART 12 — SAFELY UNDO A PUSHED COMMIT
================================================

If the unwanted commit has already been pushed and you do NOT want
to rewrite Git history:

    git revert HEAD

Then push the new revert commit:
    git push

This creates a new commit that reverses the unwanted change.

