================================================
PART 14 — MULTI-MODULE MAVEN
================================================

Typical structure:

    parent-project/
    |-- pom.xml
    |-- library-core/
    |   `-- pom.xml
    `-- library-web/
        `-- pom.xml

Parent pom.xml contains:

    <packaging>pom</packaging>

    <modules>
        <module>library-core</module>
        <module>library-web</module>
    </modules>

library-web depends on library-core by adding a dependency:

    <dependency>
        <groupId>com.library</groupId>
        <artifactId>library-core</artifactId>
        <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </dependency>

Build all modules from the PARENT PROJECT ROOT:
    mvn clean package

Build order:
    library-core
    then library-web

Because library-web depends on library-core, Maven builds library-core first.

================================================
PART 15 — DOCKERFILE FOR THIS MAVEN WEB PROJECT
================================================

For a Tomcat 9 + javax.servlet WAR project:

Dockerfile:

    FROM tomcat:9.0

    COPY target/LMS.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war

    EXPOSE 8080

    CMD ["catalina.sh", "run"]

IMPORTANT:
    target/LMS.war
is the path on your PROJECT MACHINE.

    /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war
is the path INSIDE THE DOCKER CONTAINER.

You do NOT need to create /usr/local/tomcat yourself.

The Tomcat image provides that directory.

If your WAR has another name, replace LMS.war:
    COPY target/<WAR_NAME>.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war

If you copy it as ROOT.war, access the application at:
    http://localhost:<HOST_PORT>/

If you copy it as LMS.war, the context path is normally:
    http://localhost:<HOST_PORT>/LMS/

