================================================
PART 18 — DOCKER PORT CONFLICT
================================================

If you get an error that port 7070 or 8080 is already in use:

Check containers:
    docker ps

Remove an old container if necessary:
    docker rm -f lms-container

Use another host port, for example 7071:
    docker run -d -p 7071:8080 --name lms-container lms-app

Then open:
    http://localhost:7071/

Remember:
    HOST:CONTAINER

    7071:8080
means:
    laptop port 7071 -> Tomcat inside container port 8080

The container's Tomcat port remains 8080.

